  "summary": "PocketShell is a self-hosted, mobile-first remote terminal that proxies tmux-backed terminal sessions to a phone browser, with server-side task continuation, gap-only replay on reconnect, push/webhook notifications, and Noise IK end-to-end encryption, shipped as a single-file Bun binary. Evidence is documentation-only (README and deployment guide); no runtime source code appears in the slices. Evidence coverage: 162 of 318 packet slices were shown to the model; the rest were withheld by the prompt budget.",
